# KNOWN GAP — BOTH LANES silently print a RAW POINTER for ordinary code, rc 0.
#
#     auto v = []
#     v.push(mk("alp", "ha"))
#     print(v.get(0).unwrap())     # prints e.g. 187650178232992, not "alpha"
#
# The `auto` empty-collection literal mints its array before the element type is
# known, so the element is stored/read as an 8-byte scalar and a `String` comes
# back out as its pointer value. No crash, no diagnostic -- the silently-wrong
# cell.
#
# The TYPED destination is CORRECT (prints "alpha"):
#
#     Vector[String] v = []
#
# so the discriminator is the DESTINATION DECLARATION (`auto` vs typed), and the
# element type is available at the first `push` -- this is a missing
# write-through, not missing information (Layering rule 4: resolve once, write
# through).
#
# ⚠ DISTINCT from the two filed siblings: TODO.md:269 is a COMPREHENSION
# mis-typing its accumulator on the SELF-HOST lane; TODO.md:960 is a QUALIFIED
# variant-ctor array-literal argument, also self-host. This one needs neither a
# comprehension nor an enum constructor, and it is WRONG ON THE RUST LANE TOO.
#
# ⚠ ggdef (the definitional oracle) says `2` / `alpha!` for the equivalent
# shape -- so BOTH real lanes agree on a WRONG answer, which under Core #8 is
# >=2 bugs and never a parity pass.
#
# INTENDED (asserted below): prints 2 then alpha.
# Measured 2026-08-24 by R44 Track-K brief-review pass 6, orchestrator-verified.

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    auto v = []
    v.push(mk("alp", "ha"))
    v.push(mk("bet", "a"))
    print(v.len())
    print(v.get(0).unwrap())
